@@ -2,6 +2,32 @@

 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries an API key: `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys live
+in the data as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`.
+
+- `viewer`: read only (every `GET` route except `GET /audit`).
+- `cook`: as viewer, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+A request without a key or with an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized`;
+a known key whose role may not use the route answers 403 `forbidden`. The
+key is checked before the route, so unknown routes answer 401 without a key.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request with a known key and a method other than `GET` writes an audit
+entry `{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }`, whatever its outcome
+(so refused and failed attempts are recorded too). `GET /audit` lists the
+entries newest first and is for managers only.
+
+## Routes
+
+The routes are listed under "Routes" in `README.md`; `GET /audit` returns
+the audit log (managers only).
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
